{"author":{"id":"f4e4dbe251fbd7519eab696986bae317e93a786739d6cebe9c4c1e89dd44e465"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793607859,"nonce":"wSzsviu3QuBvC0uPfTT7IeXg0Zk=","message":"Open questions from the 2026-11-02 document review, to settle before M7 starts:\n\n1. **Split M7?** The heap model (Q6, still open) gates the payment exit criterion, while loops with invariants, full `decimal` and strings do not depend on it. A possible split: M7a covers loops, full `decimal` and strings; M7b covers the heap model and verified regions and carries the payment exit criterion. Decide once Q6 is settled.\n2. **Payment target.** M6 verifies the async `ProcessPayment` with the store as a hypothesis, over records. The §5.3 target, `PayInInstallments`, is synchronous with no store calls. Must M7 also verify the async store path without records, or only §5.3?\n3. **Region exit semantics** (decide with Q4). M7 rejects contracts that ignore early exits. Yet the §5.3 target has a single `ensures` while having a `return` exit and a possible `OverflowException` from `p.Amount -= installment`. Does one `ensures` cover every exit, including `throw`? If per-exit clauses are required, update §5.3 to state its throw exit.","files":null}]}